WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.034
-Thank you, everybody.

00:00:02.034 --> 00:00:03.870
Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.304
This is it!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:07.273
You're here.
You made it. Thank you so much.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.075
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.777
Well, guys, it was a really
exciting day for the country,

00:00:11.777 --> 00:00:14.280
as we finally received
what we've been waiting for

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.748
for nine months.

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:20.286
-A historic Monday as the first
doses of the coronavirus vaccine

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.722
are being administered
to healthcare workers

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.156
across this country.

00:00:24.156 --> 00:00:26.559
-The very first dose
of Pfizer's vaccine

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:29.162
was administered to a nurse
working in Queens.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:32.665
-Yep. The first COVID vaccine
in the U.S. has been given.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:37.137
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:39.672
It was a little less exciting
when the nurse was handed a bill

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.942
for 50 grand,
but still it was, overall...

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:44.344
What a moment for the country.

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.912
Right now,
enthusiasm for the vaccine

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:48.715
is somewhere between the new PS5
and the McRib.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.550
It's that exciting.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.652
That's right, people all across
America are lining up for shots.

00:00:53.652 --> 00:00:55.488
Normally when that happens
here in December,

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:57.090
we call it SantaCon.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.958
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.793
I read that the vaccine
needs to be stored

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:04.697
at ultra-cold temperatures,
around negative-100 degrees.

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:07.399
In response, UPS workers
looked at their shorts and said,

00:01:07.399 --> 00:01:09.569
"Yeah, this seems like
more of a FedEx thing."

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.704
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.239
But today was really special.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.841
Usually if I want to see people
on TV who've gotten injections,

00:01:15.841 --> 00:01:17.343
I have to watch Bravo.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.911
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:21.414
That's right, everybody is
excited about the vaccine.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.249
Just take a look
at the Colorado governor,

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:26.385
Jared Polis, waiting for
his state's first shipment.

00:01:26.385 --> 00:01:29.188
-Any minute now,
we're gonna hear a doorbell.

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:30.222
Is that --
That's not a doorbell.

00:01:30.222 --> 00:01:32.224
That's a knock, but okay.

00:01:32.224 --> 00:01:35.795
And then we're going to,
of course, let the vaccine in.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.764
[ Bell rings ]
Oh! There we go!

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:40.199
[ Door motor whirring ]

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:44.103
This is the Pfizer vaccine,
arriving here in Colorado.

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:48.441
To end the pandemic.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.176
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.877
[ Cymbal crash ]

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:57.349
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:57.349 --> 00:01:59.318
-It got awkward when
the delivery guy was like,

00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:01.287
"Hemorrhoid cream
for Governor Polis?"

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.890
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.091
Did you guys hear about this?

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:07.227
Yesterday, it came out
that White House staffers

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:08.895
would get the vaccine early.

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:12.631
But then Trump backtracked
and tweeted that they wouldn't.

00:02:12.631 --> 00:02:14.166
Come on, just give it to them.
What's the difference?

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:15.234
There's only three people left

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:16.502
working in the White House
anyway.

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:18.771
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, Trump said his people

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.406
don't need
any special treatment.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:22.375
Then he went back
to pardoning all of them.

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:23.642
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.642 --> 00:02:24.944
Some more news from Washington.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:27.946
Government officials say
that Russians managed to hack

00:02:27.946 --> 00:02:30.582
Homeland Security,
along with the U.S. Treasury

00:02:30.582 --> 00:02:32.585
and Commerce departments.

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:35.354
Americans heard that and
they were like, "That's all?

00:02:35.354 --> 00:02:38.691
Must've been Russia's
Bring Your Child to Work Day."

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.359
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:42.161
I think Russia has hacked
just about everything there is.

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.629
I mean, what's next?

00:02:43.629 --> 00:02:46.699
"We now access information from
Blockbuster Video database."

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.270
"Why you rent 'Lethal Weapon'
six times in 1998?"

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.304
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.304 --> 00:02:53.973
Yep, they hacked
Homeland Security.

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.574
That's not a great sign

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:58.544
that our Homeland Security
needs a Homeland Security.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:02:59.945
How did they hack
Homeland Security?

00:02:59.945 --> 00:03:02.214
That's like ADT calling you
and being like,

00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:05.718
"Someone broke in! Help!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:07.854
Don't worry, though.
Today Trump appointed a new head

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:10.156
of Homeland Security --
Macaulay Culkin.

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:11.824
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:13.059
Hey, here's
a big election story.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.761
Today, members of
the Electoral College

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:17.396
officially cast their votes
for president.

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:19.332
Yeah, super exciting,
if you happened to miss

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:21.734
the 75 other times
Trump's lost the election.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.569
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:25.971
Changing gears here, I heard
about another sports team

00:03:25.971 --> 00:03:27.440
that's decided
to change its name.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.541
Watch this.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:30.576
-A major turning point
for Cleveland's

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:32.611
Major League baseball team.

00:03:32.611 --> 00:03:35.414
The franchise is expected
to drop "Indians,"

00:03:35.414 --> 00:03:38.350
a nickname it's had since 1915.

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:39.786
-Yeah.
But this is weird.

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:42.188
They're now going to be called
the Cleveland Football Team.

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:46.893
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.661
You know, when it comes
to baseball team names,

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:50.263
just play it safe
and name yourself after a bird

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:51.731
or a sock color.

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:52.898
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:56.068
No? Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.068 --> 00:03:57.970
Collectively, yeah.
Thank you.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:01.740
Red sock, blue sock, blue bird?
Yeah.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:03.276
Yeah, the team said
they just wanted to wait

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:04.743
for the right time,
which, for them,

00:04:04.743 --> 00:04:06.779
was about five months
after everyone else did it.

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:07.914
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:09.415
Well, guys,
Christmas is next week,

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:11.984
and out in California,
I heard that two undercover cops

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:14.720
have been dressing up
as Santa and his elf

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:17.022
to help catch shoplifters.

00:04:17.022 --> 00:04:18.457
Yeah, nothing says
Christmas spirit

00:04:18.457 --> 00:04:21.427
like watching Santa
Tase a shoplifter.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:24.430
You know one cop was like,
"Why can't you be the elf?"

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.665
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.665 --> 00:04:31.136
"All right."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.136 --> 00:04:33.940
"I think we're about
the same height, same build."

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.775
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:38.544
"I'm the elf?
Okay."

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:41.047
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:43.082
"There's not assigned positions.
You know, we could always..."

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:45.584
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.584 --> 00:04:48.454
"Oh, yeah.
I understand.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:51.157
You're Santa, though.
All right.

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:54.526
You're Santa, and I'm the elf.
Okay."

00:04:54.526 --> 00:04:56.228
A Santa and an elf
fighting crime.

00:04:56.228 --> 00:04:57.496
Come on.
How is that not a movie

00:04:57.496 --> 00:04:58.731
starring The Rock
and Kevin Hart?

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:02.335
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:06.438
Of course, Kevin would be Santa,
and The Rock would be the elf.

00:05:06.438 --> 00:05:08.507
Whatever.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.507 --> 00:05:09.875
And finally, the other day,
in Ukraine,

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:11.744
it got pretty icy outside,
and one woman

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:13.546
had a lot of trouble
on the sidewalk.

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:15.882
Watch this.

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:18.951
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:27.193
No, look at the --

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:29.128
No!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:32.098
Oh, my --

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:33.599
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:35.701
[ Cymbals crash ]
Yo.

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:36.836
That's basically
what it looks like

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.571
when Trump's lawyers
go to court.

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:40.038
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.038 --> 00:05:41.674
In Ukraine,
that's called the treadmill.

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:42.674
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.674 --> 00:05:43.976
Don't worry.
The woman is fine,

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:45.678
and she hopes to be home
by April.

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:47.280
Guys, a quick reminder.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.882
I have this new
children's book out,

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.650
called "5 More Sleeps
'til Christmas."

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.319
Hold your applause to the e--

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:54.920
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:57.590
Hold the drums,
hold all the noise

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:00.292
until you really need
to get it out, you know?

00:06:00.292 --> 00:06:01.927
But anyway, it's no big deal.

00:06:01.927 --> 00:06:04.897
It's currently the number-one...
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:07.333
..."New York Times" best-seller.
No big deal.

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:10.469
Anyways, we're doing
a very cool thing with Target

00:06:10.469 --> 00:06:11.837
and FAO Schwarz this week.

00:06:11.837 --> 00:06:14.706
So if you buy the book
at Target or target.com

00:06:14.706 --> 00:06:17.109
now through Wednesday.

00:06:17.109 --> 00:06:20.346
So today, tomorrow,
and Wednesday?

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:22.014
FAO Schwarz will donate a toy

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:24.216
to St. Jude
Children's Research Hospital.

00:06:24.216 --> 00:06:28.254
So you get a book at Target,
you get a toy for a kid.

00:06:28.254 --> 00:06:29.789
I appreciate those guys
doing that.

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:31.824
Guys, we have exactly
five shows left

00:06:31.824 --> 00:06:34.193
before we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time for that

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:35.695
beloved "Tonight Show"
tradition.

00:06:35.695 --> 00:06:39.431
It's time for
"12 Days of Christmas Sweaters"!

00:06:39.431 --> 00:06:41.700
-♪ 12 days
of Christmas sweaters ♪

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:45.805
♪ 5 days left ♪

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:48.340
-That is right.
Every show between now

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:51.110
and Christmas, we'll be giving
one lucky audience member

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:53.278
a ravishing Christmas sweater

00:06:53.278 --> 00:06:55.080
from the Countdown
to Christmas Cabinet.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.349
That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:59.084
Now, since there are
five shows left,

00:06:59.084 --> 00:07:01.587
let's open door number 5.

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:03.322
I see that's a big door
right there.

00:07:03.322 --> 00:07:06.292
Yes, that's the one.

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:09.095
Whoa, whoa, wait, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:10.596
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:12.364
♪♪

00:07:12.364 --> 00:07:14.100
Holy moly.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.667
That is something else.

00:07:15.667 --> 00:07:19.605
That is --
That is subtle, I guess.

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:21.574
No, it's the opposite of subtle.

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:22.808
Wow.
That is a --

00:07:22.808 --> 00:07:26.812
That is an upchuck of Christmas
is what it is.

00:07:26.812 --> 00:07:29.715
[ Laughter ]
That's what the label says.

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:32.851
Let's see who is going home
with tonight's sweater.

00:07:32.851 --> 00:07:34.020
Everyone,
look at your seat number.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.554
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:07:35.554 --> 00:07:37.156
Quest, can I get
a drumroll, please?

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:41.127
[ Drumroll ]

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:42.595
2-2-6!

00:07:42.595 --> 00:07:43.662
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:43.662 --> 00:07:46.098
Hey, come on down!

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:50.669
♪♪

00:07:50.669 --> 00:07:52.938
Hello! Hello!

00:07:52.938 --> 00:07:54.106
Nice to meet you.

00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:55.574
What is your name,
and where are you from?

00:07:55.574 --> 00:07:58.410
-Hi! I'm Masha, and I'm from
Providence, Rhode Island.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.446
-Hey, Providence, Rhode Island!
That's what I'm talking about.

00:08:01.446 --> 00:08:03.382
Do you have anything like this?

00:08:03.382 --> 00:08:05.284
-I do not.
This is amazing.

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:07.186
-Yeah.
-Can I --

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:08.520
-It looks like
you are trying it on.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:10.689
This is unbelievable.
You have to.

00:08:10.689 --> 00:08:13.058
-Oh, my gosh.
-Yeah. It's so exciting.

00:08:13.058 --> 00:08:14.459
Look at this.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:14.459 --> 00:08:16.695
Are you kidding?
Are you joking me?

00:08:16.695 --> 00:08:18.531
You look gorgeous.

00:08:18.531 --> 00:08:19.565
All right, super model.

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:21.833
Thank you so much.
Congrats again.

00:08:21.833 --> 00:08:23.569
Let's give
our audience member a --

00:08:23.569 --> 00:08:24.936
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:24.936 --> 00:08:27.406
We'll be right back
with Gal Gadot, everybody.

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:29.208
Come on back.
That was great!

00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:31.377
You look fantastic.

00:08:31.377 --> 00:08:41.387
♪♪

